    "org_modeling": {
      "how": "Paste strategy_text into the strategy box and enter design_criteria in Compare options. Upload the org file there; it is not part of this packet.",
      "strategy_text": "Who we serve: Airlines, freight forwarders and food-service customers who need reliable turnarounds at scale.\nThe outcome we sell: Aircraft and cargo that leave on time, safely, with nothing left behind.\nThe profit formula: Paid per unit handled; margin comes from labour productivity and renewal pricing.\nThe moat: Licences, network breadth and judgement built over years in safety-critical work.\nThe scale logic: Each new station is cheaper to bring up once the operating routines are standard.\n\nDesign principles:\nP1 Decisions are made at the station, by one named role.\nP2 Standard work is written once and run everywhere.\nP3 AI takes the rule-based work; people keep the judgement.\nP4 Capability is built ahead of growth, not after it.\n\nCapability priorities (highest value exposure first):\nCAP-03 Technology, Data & AI — maturity 2.25/4, unknown, 30% of economic weight. Priority move: Scale the digital core + drive data standardisation + AI CoE globally.\nCAP-01 Gateway / Hub Services — maturity 2.5/4, unknown, 21% of economic weight. Priority move: Scale hub-of-the-future globally + close the safety-culture gap urgently.\nCAP-04 Commercial Leadership — maturity 3/4, unknown, 22% of economic weight. Priority move: Fill the commercial bench + activate global accounts + per-country growth plans.\nCAP-05 Enterprise Leadership — maturity 3/4, unknown, 12% of economic weight. Priority move: Scale leadership development globally + close the bottom-quintile long tail.\nCAP-06 Human Capital & Enabling — maturity 2.75/4, unknown, 5% of economic weight. Priority move: Build people analytics + activate the engagement framework at scale.\nCAP-02 Food & Catering Solutions — maturity 3.5/4, unknown, 10% of economic weight. Priority move: Monetise waste-intelligence platform + arrest the cultural decline.",
